---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    actor Steward
    participant Page as Site page<br/>app/detail/[namesite]
    participant Server as Server actions<br/>site-priority-actions.ts
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>sites_pa priority columns

    Note over Admin,DB: Covers US 2.0.12 and 2.0.13. The three scores and their saved date<br/>are columns on sites_pa. The priority is not stored.

    Note over Admin,DB: Save the three scores (US 2.0.12 AT 1, AT 5, US 2.0.13 AT 3)
    Admin->>Page: Enter points for abuses, biological imperatives<br/>and time since the last visit, then Save
    Page->>Server: saveSitePriorityScores(siteId, scores)
    Server->>Server: Check caller is Admin from the signed-in session<br/>(app_metadata role is admin and the account is approved)
    Server->>Server: Check each score is a whole number from 0 to 5
    alt Caller is not Admin, for example a Steward<br/>who sends the request directly (US 2.0.12 AT 5)
        Server-->>Page: Refuse (403). Scores stay the same
        Page-->>Steward: Show "Only an Admin can change the scores"
    else Caller is Admin
        Server->>DB: Update the sites_pa row with the service role.<br/>Set priority_saved_at to now and priority_saved_by to the caller
        DB-->>Server: Saved row
        Server-->>Page: Saved. The reminder is absent (US 2.0.13 AT 3)
    end

    Note over Admin,DB: Show the priority (US 2.0.12 AT 2, AT 3, AT 4, US 2.0.13 AT 1, AT 2, AT 4)
    Steward->>Page: Open a Site page
    Page->>Server: getSitePriority(siteId)
    Server->>Server: Check session and approved account
    alt No valid session or account not approved
        Server-->>Page: Refuse (401)
        Page-->>Steward: Go to /login
    else Access allowed
        Server->>DB: Read the priority columns of the sites_pa row
        DB-->>Server: Three scores and priority_saved_at
        Server->>Server: computeVisitPriority(scores): the sum of the three scores, 0 to 15.<br/>Same scores give the same priority
        opt Caller is Admin and priority_saved_at is more than one year ago
            Server->>Server: Add needsReassessment = true (US 2.0.13)
        end
        Server-->>Page: Priority and three scores. needsReassessment only for Admins
        Page-->>Steward: Show priority and three scores. No reminder (US 2.0.13 AT 4)
        Note over Admin,Page: For an Admin, the page also shows the reminder when<br/>needsReassessment is true (US 2.0.13 AT 1, AT 2)
    end

    Note over Admin,DB: The server calculates the priority and the reminder, so each client shows the same values.<br/>"Time since the last visit" is a score that an Admin types. Open question for Frank:<br/>he has not confirmed that the priority is the sum of the three scores.
